{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-155556",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The variable $a$ is being *divided* by $4.$ To isolate $a$ and remove the negative sign, we *multiply* by $-4.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{a}{4}\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-2 \\\\ (-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{4})\\,\\, & <\\,\\,(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{4})\\,\\, & <\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince two negative numbers multiply to give a positive number, we first cancel the negatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{4}) & <8 \\\\ (\\cancel{-}4)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}\\frac{a}{4}) & <8 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{a}{4} & <8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $4$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot \\frac{a}{4} & <8 \\\\ \\frac{4a}{4} & <8 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}a}{\\cancel{4}} & <8 \\\\ a & <8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a<8.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192536/assets/ebda9e955c2613aa9e65b950ac80ad7ec4e52d6db6fdcce76cc2f89bbc20b0d4.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-155556\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p> The variable <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"28\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is being <em>divided</em> by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"29\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> To isolate <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"30\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and remove the negative sign, we <em>multiply</em> by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"31\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mn>4.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </p>\n<p>Remember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"32\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 12em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-tstrut></mjx-tstrut></mjx-mtd><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: left; padding-left: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"></mjx-mi><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom></mjx-mstyle></mjx-texatom><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class